# PRD and issue graph approval

## Summary
The public orchestrator continues from human-approved explanation to a PRD job and then a separate issue-planning session. It requests execution approval for the PRD and graph together. No executor or preflight starts here.

## Key behavior
- `generatePrd`, `generateIssues`, `continuePlanning`, and `handlePlanningResponse` are public module entrypoints. Role instructions combine bundled output contracts with project overrides; jobs capture model, instruction hash, repository commit, source revisions, and session identity.
- Artifacts live under `.ralph/features/<run-id>/prd-<generation>/PRD.md` and `graph-<generation>/{graph.json,issues/*.md}`. The state record is the current revision pointer. Generation numbers and artifact revisions are distinct; prior directories are retained.
- The orchestrator records publication intent and atomically renames each complete draft directory before selecting its revision. A crash can leave an unselected directory; it cannot select a partial bundle.
- Issue graphs require schema version 1, an exact PRD revision reference, unique IDs/paths, known dependencies, a DAG, acceptance criteria and testable behaviors. Each local Markdown issue must contain context, implementation, tests, acceptance criteria and dependencies. Topological order drives the numbered approval presentation.
- The graph hash covers graph metadata and all issue contents. Approval re-reads published files and binds the current PRD and graph hashes to a correlated human request/message and timestamp. Revisions regenerate both artifacts, invalidate old approval and preserve prior files/events.
- Assistant responses, missing/malformed output, stale requests and interrupted/late jobs cannot authorize execution. Timeouts interrupt and cancel the correlated session.

## Code references
- `src/commands/orchestrator.ts`, `src/core/orchestrator.ts` — automatic continuation and execution-intent boundary.
- `src/planning/prd.ts`, `src/planning/issues.ts` — generation and combined human approval.
- `src/planning/graph.ts`, `src/planning/generation.ts` — validation, job correlation and atomic revision publication.
- `src/state/run-store.ts` — compare-and-swap persistence and approval invalidation.
- `skills/create-prd/SKILL.md`, `skills/to-issues/SKILL.md` — bundled local artifact contracts.
- `tests/integration/04-planning.test.ts` — diamond DAG, revision approval, invalid graph and interruption regressions.

## Related
- [Feature interview](feature-interview.md)
- [Workflow recovery](workflow-recovery.md)

## Notes
Production human provenance remains unsupported by the existing adapter. Fixtures exercise the public command and real SDK mapping with host-provided human responses. Preflight/scheduling and interrupted planning continuation are downstream work. Native Linux/Windows and live human/model approval checks were not run.

